      "name": "bracket_limit_exit",
      "source": "Pyne-defined bracket-exit strategy fixture with a Pine-equivalent scaffold for external TradingView export comparison.",
      "script": "strategy(\"Pine Equivalent Bracket Limit\", overlay=True, initial_capital=1000, pyramiding=0, process_orders_on_close=True)\nstrategy.entry(\"Long\", strategy.long, qty=1, when=bar_index == 0, price=close)\nstrategy.exit(\"Bracket\", from_entry=\"Long\", stop=9, limit=12)\nplot(strategy.position_size, \"Position\")\nplot(strategy.equity, \"Equity\")\nplot(strategy.netprofit, \"Net Profit\")\nplot(strategy.openprofit, \"Open Profit\")\nplot(strategy.closedtrades, \"Closed Trades\")\n",
      "pine_equivalent": "//@version=5\nstrategy(\"Pine Equivalent Bracket Limit\", overlay=true, initial_capital=1000, pyramiding=0, process_orders_on_close=true)\nif bar_index == 0\n    strategy.entry(\"Long\", strategy.long, qty=1)\nstrategy.exit(\"Bracket\", from_entry=\"Long\", stop=9, limit=12)\nplot(strategy.position_size, \"Position\")\nplot(strategy.equity, \"Equity\")\nplot(strategy.netprofit, \"Net Profit\")\nplot(strategy.openprofit, \"Open Profit\")\nplot(strategy.closedtrades, \"Closed Trades\")\n",
      "pine_equivalent_notes": [
        "The Pyne entry pins price=close to match process_orders_on_close-style Pine fills.",
        "The second bar touches only the limit side of the bracket, avoiding same-bar stop/limit ambiguity."
